{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"a381b2c39b98108664e15f33560bc953b2ebc92537e93c9e21def3f27758b1c7","packTokens":2561,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":385,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":710,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1146,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Import procurement and receiving data, and map PO lines to lots and pens with traceability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Forecast projected market dates and target weights from incoming animal data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Track feed inventory, stock movements, wastage, and forecasts across multiple time horizons.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Create and optimize rations, including ingredient proportions, nutritional values, and costs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Generate pen-level feeding plans and log actual feeding activities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Record lot weight measurements and maintain a time series of readings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Calculate feed-to-gain metrics and update them when feeding or weight events are recorded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide dashboards and reports for lot, pen, ration, inventory, feeding, and performance metrics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report with filters and CSV or PDF export.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Create sample or mock data to support the system.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Which user roles and access boundaries are required for operational records, cost/performance views, imports, and data entry?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No role distinctions; all users can view and operate all product areas.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Should the wastage ratio represent only forecasted/estimated losses, or should actual wastage also be recorded as a separate stock movement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the ratio to consumption estimates and projections; record actual wastage separately only when entered as a movement.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"When one pen contains multiple lots, how should a feeding activity's actual quantity and cost be attributed to lot-level metrics?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require the operator to enter a separate activity quantity for each affected lot.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Should feed-to-gain calculations use feed on an as-fed basis or adjust feed consumption to dry matter?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use as-fed pounds for total feed consumed and FCR, converting entered inventory units to pounds as needed.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Does 'lot-level profitability/ROI' require more than the specified feed cost per unit of weight gain?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Report feed cost per pound of gain only; do not label it full ROI or profitability.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"What should ration optimization treat as its objective and constraints, and should a suggested ration ever be applied automatically?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Present feasible low-cost mixes for user-specified nutritional targets or constraints; require the user to select a suggestion before using it.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Must each actual feeding activity be linked to an existing feed plan, or may operators record feedings when no plan exists?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Allow an activity against a pen and date without a plan; link it to a plan when one exists so variance can be shown.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How should lot-level total weight gain be derived when measurements record an average weight and a number of animals weighed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Calculate lot total gain from the average-weight change multiplied by the lot headcount applicable at the measurement dates.\",\n  \"by\": \"Ahsan (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build a responsive feedlot web app that lets users preview and synchronize mock purchase-order and receiving records, review returned row details and outcomes, trace purchase-order lines to lots and pens, and keep unresolved records unavailable for pen operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide lot forecasts with editable target-weight and gain-rate assumptions, using measured ADG when available and the configured default otherwise, and display returned recommendations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Provide inventory screens for feed-item details and stock movements, including separately entered actual wastage; let users configure the wastage ratio for estimates and projections and review labeled daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual projected balances without low-stock alerts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Let users create and view rations with ingredient proportions, nutrition values, intended animal type or weight range, and calculated cost per pound; compare feasible optimized mixes against user targets using recorded costs and nutrition, ordered by lowest cost, and require selection before applying a suggestion.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Let users generate and review dated, pen-specific feeding plans using a selected ration, daily bunk rate, and pen animal count, showing plan status and feeding details; display planned and actual quantities, variance, and returned adjustments when actual intake is available.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Let users record feeding activities by pen and date, with an optional plan link and a separate actual quantity for each affected lot in a multi-lot pen; display returned costs, energy, inventory and lot consumption, plan variance, and save or shortage outcomes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Let users record, view, edit, and delete lot weight measurements, displaying dated readings, time series, returned metrics, and validation errors; display lot feed-to-gain metrics based on applicable headcounts and as-fed pounds, and refresh metrics after feeding or weight events are saved, edited, or deleted.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Provide the public FeedToGainCalculator.calculate method to calculate days on feed, total lot gain, ADG, as-fed feed pounds, FCR, feed cost per pound of gain, and projected market date from supplied receiving, feeding, weight, headcount, and target-weight data, using configured default gain when ADG is unavailable.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Provide lot- and pen-level dashboards with returned operational and performance metrics, including identified best- and worst-performing lots, and operational reports comparing pen consumption, lot performance, ration usage, plan alignment, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a feed-to-gain report comparing lot ADG, FCR, and feed cost per pound of gain, with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters; use the latest weight reading in range and feeding events up to that reading, display returned errors for invalid filters, and allow CSV and PDF export of filtered results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Let users load a clearly labeled, separate demo dataset on demand and display added, already-present, and failed record outcomes, including partial-load status without labeling a partial load complete.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a project and demo area presenting the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demonstration, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Expose the same product areas, operational records, cost and performance views, import screens, and data-entry controls to all users without role-dependent restrictions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure every page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths without page-level horizontal overflow, and use touch-sized controls on narrow phone layouts.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}